course: dictionary
lesson: 2761
title: Disclosure: telling what was hidden
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A disclosure is the act of telling something that was secret or private. The word helps you think of a door being opened, so something hidden is now known. «Telling the owner about a weakness without using it is called responsible disclosure.» The weakness was hidden, and telling the owner about it is the disclosure.
explain: Context clues show you the meaning. Look at the words around disclosure: «make a disclosure», «full disclosure», «public disclosure». Full means everything, and public means for everyone to know, so a disclosure is information being made known. Try your meaning in the sentence: "telling the owner about a weakness" fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Disclosure is also a serious word in safety. A disclosure can be a child telling a trusted adult that something harmful is happening to them. When that happens, the adult must act to keep the child safe. If something worries you, tell a trusted adult such as a parent or teacher.
fact: A disclosure is telling people something that was secret or private.
fact: A disclosure can also be a fact or piece of information that is made known.
fact: In law and business, a disclosure means officially giving information.
fact: In safety, a disclosure is when a child tells a trusted adult about something harmful happening to them.
fact: «Responsible disclosure» means telling the owner about a weakness without using it.
exercise: «Telling the owner about a weakness without using it is called responsible disclosure.» What does disclosure mean here? | *Telling someone about something that was hidden | Deleting a website | Using a weakness to win a prize | Hiding a weakness forever
exercise: What does «full disclosure» mean? | *Giving all the information, with nothing held back | Closing a door tightly | Dressing up in a costume | Keeping one small secret
exercise: A child tells a trusted teacher that something harmful is happening to them. What is this called? | A password | A competition | A puzzle | *A disclosure
test: «Public disclosure» means the information is made known to whom? | Nobody, it stays hidden | Only one person in a locked room | *Everyone | Only the people who wrote it
test: A child makes a disclosure to you. What is the best thing to do? | *Stay calm, listen, and get help from a trusted adult | Ask them to make it up | Tell them to keep it secret | Laugh and change the subject
exam: Which sentence uses disclosure to mean information made known? | The disclosure of the cake was very tasty | The dog made a disclosure about the ball | A disclosure is a type of bicycle | *The company's new disclosure showed its profits had fallen
